new_sec44 = """\\subsection{Unified Young--Gr\\"{o}nwall--Lyapunov Extrapolation Bound and Per-Seed Spectral Norm Audit}
While Theorem~\\ref{thm:uub} guarantees that individual trajectories remain globally bounded for any $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} > 0$, bounding the tracking error $e(t) = [\\delta q(t); \\delta p(t)] = \\hat{z}(t) - z^*(t)$ between two trajectories requires analyzing the nonlinear force difference $\\Delta F_{\\mathrm{nl}}(\\hat{q}, q^*) = -\\big(\\nabla_q V_{\\mathrm{mlp}}(\\hat{q}) - \\nabla_q V_{\\mathrm{mlp}}(q^*)\\big) + \\big(F_{\\mathrm{ext}}(\\hat{q}) - F_{\\mathrm{ext}}(q^*)\\big)$. Partitioning $W_{\\mathrm{pot}}$ into its convex modes ($s_i = +1 > 0$, where $s_i \\mathrm{sech}^2(\\cdot)w_i w_i^T \\succeq 0$ adds to restoring stiffness) and non-convex modes ($s_i = -0.65 < 0$, submatrix $W_{\\mathrm{pot},-} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times 3}$), we define the two-sided Lipschitz constant $L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}}$ and one-sided non-convex monotonicity constant $L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)}$:
\\begin{align}
L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}} &= \\underbrace{\\frac{1}{d}\\|W_{\\mathrm{pot}}\\|_2^2}_{L_{V,\\mathrm{full}}} + c_f \\beta_q, \\label{eq:lnl_full} \\\\
L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)} &= \\underbrace{\\frac{0.65}{d}\\|W_{\\mathrm{pot},-}\\|_2^2}_{L_{V,-}} + c_f \\beta_q, \\label{eq:lnl_neg}
\\end{align}
where $c_f \\beta_q = 0.45 \\times 0.35 = 0.1575$. Along the error dynamics, differentiating $W(e) = \\frac{1}{2}e^T P e = \\frac{1}{2}\\|e\\|_P^2$ generates both a position inner product $\\epsilon\\delta q^T \\Delta F_{\\mathrm{nl}}(\\hat{q}, q^*) \\le \\epsilon L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)}\\|\\delta q\\|_2^2$ and a velocity-force cross-term $\\delta p^T \\Delta F_{\\mathrm{nl}}(\\hat{q}, q^*) \\le L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}}\\|\\delta q\\|_2 \\|\\delta p\\|_2$. Bounding the combined cross-term $(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})\\|\\delta q\\|_2 \\|\\delta p\\|_2$ via Young's inequality (Appendix~\\ref{app:proof_thm3}) reveals a fundamental mathematical distinction:
\\begin{enumerate}
    \\item \\textbf{Why Strict Incremental Contraction Fails on Trained Checkpoints ($0/10$ Seeds):} Even though $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} = 0.35 > L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)} = 0.2242 \\pm 0.0237$ holds on $10/10$ default seeds, absorbing the velocity-force cross-term $(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})\\|\\delta q\\|_2 \\|\\delta p\\|_2$ into $-(\\gamma - \\epsilon)\\|\\delta p\\|_2^2$ via Young's inequality requires the strict small-gain condition $(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2 < 2\\epsilon(\\gamma - \\epsilon)(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)})$. Because $\\gamma = 0.15$ and $c_f\\beta_q = 0.1575$, $(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2 = 0.1489 \\pm 0.0273 \\gg 2\\epsilon(\\gamma - \\epsilon)(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)}) = 0.00141 \\pm 0.00027$. Consequently, \\textbf{neither the default ($\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.35$) nor the uncapped ($\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.10$) configuration is incrementally contractive in $W(e)$}.
    \\item \\textbf{Finite-Horizon Young--Gr\\"{o}nwall Regime with Two-Trajectory UUB Capping ($10/10$ Seeds):} Choosing Young's parameter $\\eta = \\gamma - \\epsilon > 0$ cancels the positive $\\|\\delta p\\|_2^2$ cross-term and yields a finite-horizon Gr\\"{o}nwall growth rate $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} = K_{\\mathrm{Young}} / (\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - \\epsilon^2) > 0$, where $K_{\\mathrm{Young}} = \\frac{(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2}{4(\\gamma - \\epsilon)} - \\epsilon(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)}) > 0$. In the default bounded-horizon setting ($h_k = 0.35, \\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} = 0.35$), $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} = 1.5185 \\pm 0.2823\\text{ s}^{-1}$ and $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}}h_k = 0.531 \\pm 0.099 = O(1)$, yielding a tight RUL error bound ($33.25 \\pm 3.22$ cycles). Conversely, in the uncapped full-horizon setting ($h_{\\max}=\\infty, \\bar{h}_k=3.743, \\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.10$), $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} = 3.7179 \\pm 0.6606\\text{ s}^{-1}$ and $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}}\\bar{h}_k \\approx 13.9$, so the exponential Gr\\"{o}nwall bound blows up ($\\sim 10^6\\text{--}10^8$) and saturates at the global two-trajectory UUB ceiling $\\bar{R}_{\\mathrm{UUB}} = R_\\infty + R_\\infty^*$.
\\end{enumerate}

\\begin{theorem}[Unified Gap Extrapolation Error Bound]
\\label{thm:extrap_bound}
Let $\\hat{z}(t) = [\\hat{q}(t); \\hat{p}(t)]$ denote the continuous-time model trajectory of Eq.~\\eqref{eq:eom} on $t \\in [t_k, t_k + h_k]$ with $\\|\\tilde{F}(\\hat{q})\\|_2 \\le L_V + F_{\\max}$ ($L_V = d^{-1/2}\\|W_{\\mathrm{pot}}\\|_2, F_{\\max} = c_f\\sqrt{d}$), and let $z^*(t) = [q^*(t); \\dot{q}^*(t)]$ denote the target trajectory satisfying $\\ddot{q}^*(t) + \\gamma \\dot{q}^*(t) + \\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}(q^*(t) - q_k) = \\tilde{F}(q^*(t)) + r_{\\mathrm{model}}(t)$ with uniformly bounded model residual $\\|r_{\\mathrm{model}}(t)\\|_2 \\le \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{model}}$. Let $e_{q,k} = \\|q_k - q^*(t_k)\\|_2$ and $e_{v,k} = \\|\\dot{q}_k - \\dot{q}^*(t_k)\\|_2$. Assume both initial displacement states $\\tilde{\\hat{z}}(t_k) = [0; \\dot{q}_k]$ and $\\tilde{z}^*(t_k) = [q^*(t_k) - q_k; \\dot{q}^*(t_k)]$ lie within their respective Theorem~\\ref{thm:uub} absorbing balls of radii $R_\\infty = \\sqrt{\\frac{2C_F}{\\mu\\lambda_{\\min}(P)}}$ and $R_\\infty^* = \\sqrt{\\frac{2C_F^*}{\\mu\\lambda_{\\min}(P)}} = R_\\infty\\frac{L_V + F_{\\max} + \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{model}}}{L_V + F_{\\max}}$, where $C_F^* = \\big(\\frac{\\epsilon}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}} + \\frac{1}{2(\\gamma - \\epsilon)}\\big)(L_V + F_{\\max} + \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{model}})^2$, so that $\\|\\hat{z}(t) - z^*(t)\\|_2 \\le R_\\infty + R_\\infty^* \\triangleq \\bar{R}_{\\mathrm{UUB}}$ for all $t \\in [t_k, t_k + h_k]$.
\\begin{enumerate}
    \\item \\textbf{Small-Gain Contractive Regime ($(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2 < 2\\epsilon(\\gamma - \\epsilon)(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)})$, Satisfied on $0/10$ Trained Seeds):} If the small-gain condition holds, setting $\\eta = \\frac{\\gamma - \\epsilon}{2}$ yields $c_{q,\\mathrm{net}} = \\epsilon(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)}) - \\frac{(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2}{2(\\gamma - \\epsilon)} > 0$, $c_{p,\\mathrm{net}} = \\frac{\\gamma - \\epsilon}{2} > 0$, and net contraction rate $\\mu_{\\mathrm{net}} = \\frac{2\\min(c_{q,\\mathrm{net}}, c_{p,\\mathrm{net}})}{\\lambda_{\\max}(P)} > 0$:
    \\begin{align}
    &\\big|\\hat{\\mu}_{k+1} - y^*(t_{k+1})\\big| \\le \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{probe}} \\nonumber \\\\
    &\\quad + L_g \\kappa_P e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\mu_{\\mathrm{net}} h_k}\\sqrt{e_{q,k}^2 + h_k^2 e_{v,k}^2} \\nonumber \\\\
    &\\quad + L_g \\frac{1 - e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\mu_{\\mathrm{net}} h_k}}{\\frac{1}{2}\\mu_{\\mathrm{net}}}\\big(\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{model}} + C_{\\mathrm{symp}}\\delta t^2\\big),
    \\label{eq:thm3_bound}
    \\end{align}
    where $\\kappa_P = \\sqrt{\\lambda_{\\max}(P)/\\lambda_{\\min}(P)}$, $\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{probe}}$ is the baseline in-distribution probe RMSE, and $L_g$ is the RUL probe Lipschitz factor.
    \\item \\textbf{Finite-Horizon Young--Gr\\"{o}nwall Regime ($(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2 \\ge 2\\epsilon(\\gamma - \\epsilon)(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)})$, Governing $10/10$ Trained Seeds for Both $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.35$ and $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.10$):} Setting $\\eta = \\gamma - \\epsilon$ yields $K_{\\mathrm{Young}} = \\frac{(\\epsilon\\gamma + L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}})^2}{4(\\gamma - \\epsilon)} - \\epsilon(\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)}) > 0$ and Gr\\"{o}nwall growth exponent $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} = \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Young}}}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}} - \\epsilon^2} > 0$:
    \\begin{align}
    &\\big|\\hat{\\mu}_{k+1} - y^*(t_{k+1})\\big| \\le \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{probe}} + L_g \\min\\!\\Bigg\\{R_\\infty + R_\\infty^*, \\nonumber \\\\
    &\\quad \\kappa_P e^{\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} h_k}\\sqrt{e_{q,k}^2 + h_k^2 e_{v,k}^2} \\nonumber \\\\
    &\\quad + \\frac{e^{\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} h_k} - 1}{\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}}}\\big(\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{model}} + C_{\\mathrm{symp}}\\delta t^2\\big)\\Bigg\\}.
    \\label{eq:thm3_gronwall}
    \\end{align}
\\end{enumerate}
\\end{theorem}
\\emph{Proof and Reproducible Per-Seed Verification:} See Appendix~\\ref{app:proof_thm3} and Table~\\ref{tab:thm3_per_seed}. Across the 10 trained FD001 checkpoints ($\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.35, h_k=0.35$, Table~\\ref{tab:thm3_per_seed} Panel~A), the measured parameters are $\\|W_{\\mathrm{pot}}\\|_2 = 1.3070 \\pm 0.1108$, $L_{\\mathrm{nl,full}} = 0.3724 \\pm 0.0357$, $L_{\\mathrm{nl}}^{(-)} = 0.2242 \\pm 0.0237$, $K_{\\mathrm{Young}} = 0.5218 \\pm 0.0970$, $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} = 1.5185 \\pm 0.2823\\text{ s}^{-1}$, $R_\\infty + R_\\infty^* = 162.07 \\pm 4.09$, $e_{q,k} = 0.2432 \\pm 0.0336$, $\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{model}} = 0.6306 \\pm 0.0893$, and $\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{probe}} = 12.53 \\pm 0.31$ cycles. Secant velocity alignment ($\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{kin}}$) reduces initial velocity error $e_{v,k}$ by \\textbf{$67.9\\%$} (from $2.7288 \\pm 0.5345$ to $0.8768 \\pm 0.0927$). Evaluating Eq.~\\eqref{eq:thm3_gronwall} with the directional probe sensitivity ($L_{g,\\mathrm{dir}} = 14.27 \\pm 1.02\\text{ cycles/unit}$) reduces the finite-horizon bound by \\textbf{$42.8\\%$, from $58.14 \\pm 10.65$ cycles (without $\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{kin}}$) to $33.25 \\pm 3.22$ cycles (with $\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{kin}}$)}, bracketing the empirical \\texttt{OOD 10x--20x} RMSE ($19.50 \\pm 0.54$ cycles) on all 10 seeds, whereas the worst-case operator spectral norm ($L_{g,\\mathrm{spec}} = 115.30 \\pm 6.30$) yields $179.45 \\pm 20.93$ cycles. In the uncapped full-horizon setting ($\\alpha_{\\mathrm{eff}}=0.10, \\bar{h}_k=3.743$, Table~\\ref{tab:thm3_per_seed} Panel~B), $\\nu_{\\mathrm{Young}} = 3.7179 \\pm 0.6606\\text{ s}^{-1}$ causes the Gr\\"{o}nwall term ($\\sim 10^6\\text{--}10^8$) to saturate at the UUB ceiling $R_\\infty + R_\\infty^* = 616.53 \\pm 14.95$."""
assert old_sec44 in tex, "Section 4.4 target not found"
tex = tex.replace(old_sec44, new_sec44, 1)

