old_sec45_item3 = """    \\item \\textbf{Exchangeability Assumptions and Unseen Outage Distribution Shift:} Finite-sample Mondrian validity $\\mathbb{P}(Y_{\\mathrm{test}} \\in \\mathcal{C}_{1-\\alpha} \\mid \\hat{\\mu}_{\\mathrm{test}} \\in \\mathcal{B}_b) \\ge 1 - \\alpha$ requires two conditions: (i) conditioning is on the observable predicted bin $\\hat{\\mu}_{\\mathrm{test}} \\in \\mathcal{B}_b$ (not unobserved true RUL $Y_{\\mathrm{test}}$), and (ii) calibration and test nonconformity scores within $\\mathcal{B}_b$ are exchangeable \\cite{vovk2005algorithmic, romano2019conformalized}. In standard matched calibration (Table~\\ref{tab:conformal_ablation}), validation units $\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathrm{cal}}$ are subsampled with the same outage distribution as test units. When an asset encounters an \\emph{unseen operational outage pattern} at test time (e.g., calibrating $\\hat{q}$ on in-distribution $25\\%$ MCAR validation data $\\Delta t \\in [1\\tau_0, 2\\tau_0]$ and deploying directly on unseen $10\\times\\text{--}20\\times$ blackouts without recalibration), raw residuals $|y - \\hat{\\mu}|$ violate exchangeability; however, dividing by $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{dd}}(t_k, \\Delta t_k)$ in Eq.~\\eqref{eq:drift_diff_sigma} scales the denominator by the Ornstein--Uhlenbeck diffusion rate $\\sqrt{1 + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{dd}}\\max(0, \\tilde{\\Delta t}_k - 0.25)}$, approximately restoring score exchangeability across unseen gap lengths (verified empirically in Section~\\ref{sec:exp_conformal})."""

new_sec45_item3 = """    \\item \\textbf{Exchangeability Assumptions vs.\\ Empirical Performance Under Unseen Outage Shift:} Finite-sample distribution-free Mondrian validity $\\mathbb{P}(Y_{\\mathrm{test}} \\in \\mathcal{C}_{1-\\alpha} \\mid \\hat{\\mu}_{\\mathrm{test}} \\in \\mathcal{B}_b) \\ge 1 - \\alpha$ holds formally \\emph{if and only if} (i) conditioning is on the observable predicted bin $\\hat{\\mu}_{\\mathrm{test}} \\in \\mathcal{B}_b$ and (ii) calibration and test nonconformity scores within $\\mathcal{B}_b$ are exchangeable \\cite{vovk2005algorithmic, romano2019conformalized}. In matched calibration (Table~\\ref{tab:conformal_ablation}), validation units $\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathrm{cal}}$ share the same outage distribution as test units, so exchangeability holds by construction. Conversely, when an asset encounters an \\emph{unseen operational outage pattern} at test time (e.g., calibrating $\\hat{q}$ on in-distribution $25\\%$ MCAR validation data $\\Delta t \\in [1\\tau_0, 2\\tau_0]$ and deploying directly on unseen $10\\times\\text{--}20\\times$ blackouts without recalibration), exchangeability is formally violated and \\textbf{no distribution-free finite-sample coverage guarantee holds} without importance-weighting the covariate shift. Dividing residuals by $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{dd}}(t_k, \\Delta t_k)$ in Eq.~\\eqref{eq:drift_diff_sigma} is a physics-motivated heuristic that scales the score denominator by the Ornstein--Uhlenbeck diffusion factor $\\sqrt{1 + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{dd}}\\max(0, \\tilde{\\Delta t}_k - 0.25)}$; the resulting $94.61 \\pm 1.59\\%$ coverage reported in Section~\\ref{sec:exp_conformal} is strictly \\textbf{empirical evidence} of approximate score stabilization rather than a formal guarantee under nonexchangeability."""
